debian-minerva (0.5.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Session bootstrap now follows the proven Debian/X11 session conventions,
    adapted from the Openbox project (openbox-session.in, autostart.in,
    github.com/danakj/openbox) and startxfce4 (xfce-mirror/xfce4-session):
      - private D-Bus session bus via dbus-launch when the display manager
        did not provide one;
      - /etc/xdg/openbox/environment + user environment sourcing;
      - ~/.Xresources merged with xrdb;
      - stale EWMH root properties removed before the WM starts;
      - XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=Minerva exported and imported into the systemd
        user session;
      - root window painted before the shell surface maps;
      - autostart moved to the stock Openbox --startup hook
        (/usr/bin/minerva-autostart): Minerva services first, then the
        distro openbox-autostart chain (system + user + XDG autostart spec),
        with openbox-xdg-autostart/dex as fallback runners;
      - openbox watchdog restarts the WM (with its autostart hook) if it dies.
  * Recommends += dbus-x11, dex.

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:20:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Critical parsing fix: xprop renders EWMH window ids as "#x4600007" but
    the parser stopped at the leading 'x', so the live taskbar list was
    always empty, focus detection never matched, and the shell-surface
    enforcer and minerva-doctor window scans silently matched nothing.
    All three now parse past the optional 'x' (session enforcer and doctor
    sed patterns fixed as well).
  * Session resilience: a crashed shell surface is respawned up to three
    times instead of ending the session and dropping the user at the
    login screen; logout/kill paths set an EXITING guard so respawning
    never fights teardown.
  * Security: the icon API no longer reads arbitrary absolute paths; only
    /usr/share, /usr/lib and /opt roots are served (still token-gated).

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:40:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * minerva-doctor: one-command session health report (daemon, WM, shell
    surface, browser, default apps, services, log tail) with OK/FAIL per
    subsystem; wired into the Openbox root menu.
  * Taskbar is workspace-aware: windows carry _NET_WM_DESKTOP and the dock
    shows only the current desktop (sticky windows everywhere), like XFCE/
    GNOME tasklists.
  * Real taskbar semantics: clicking a focused dock item minimizes it.
  * Power menu gains Suspend (logind/systemctl); power menu now renders
    in-surface in X11 sessions instead of opening a legacy panel window.
  * Chromium windows group under the pinned Browser dock icon (app-id
    guess aligned with the launcher catalogue).
  * UI polish towards the Aluminium reference: translucent blurred status
    bar scrim, blurred popovers/launcher/settings surfaces.
  * Openbox root menu: launcher/settings now route through the shell event
    queue; added Minerva Doctor entry.

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:05:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix E0382 in running_json(): the EWMH window id was moved into the JSON
    object and then compared for focus — the 0.4.0 source did not compile.
  * Shell-surface enforcer: a small session loop re-applies EWMH state
    (below, fullscreen, skip_taskbar/pager) to the shell surface every few
    seconds via wmctrl, so no client behaviour or missed WM rule can ever
    unpin the desktop surface; raiseOnFocus restored to yes for standard
    click-to-raise behaviour of app windows.
  * In a real session a failed app launch now shows the daemon error as a
    toast instead of silently opening a JS fallback window.

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:10:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Session v3 "single surface": the whole Minerva desktop (wallpaper, top
    bar, taskbar dock, launcher, popovers, notifications, settings) is drawn
    by ONE fullscreen shell surface (chromium --kiosk), while real
    applications run as ordinary X clients managed by Openbox. This removes
    the entire class of window-placement failures: a kiosk window is
    fullscreen by itself on any stack, and app windows get standard
    window-manager placement.
  * Dock taskbar now mirrors the window manager: EWMH _NET_CLIENT_LIST via
    xprop lists every real window; click focuses/raises, right-click closes
    (wmctrl). Super key opens the in-surface launcher through a new shell
    event queue (openbox keybind -> daemon -> shell).
  * Popovers, notifications and settings render in-surface (no more separate
    panel windows that had to be placed).
  * Standard desktop autostart: dunst (notifications), parcellite
    (clipboard), polkit authentication agent; bundled slim dark Openbox
    theme "Minerva" for app window chrome.
  * New default app set wired into Depends/Recommends and the launcher:
    xterm/xfce4-terminal, pcmanfm, mousepad, viewnior, xarchiver, galculator,
    atril, scrot.
  * docs/PRODUCT.md: full product roadmap (compositor/shell/session/services
    phases) with per-phase status and the v1.0 Wayland compositor milestone.

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Shell windows (desktop/topbar/dock) now use a fresh chromium profile per
    login so window bounds saved by an earlier broken session can never be
    restored over the placement flags and Openbox rules.
  * Session checks that openbox is still alive right after start, retries
    once, and logs the outcome plus the per-window geometry it requested,
    so placement problems are diagnosable from session.log.

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Window placement fix: chromium honours --wm-class, not --class, so the
    Openbox application rules (topbar/dock/desktop/panels) never matched and
    every shell window fell back to a centred default-sized window. Panels
    and shell windows now set --wm-class (plus --class for compatibility),
    the rc.xml rules match both WM_CLASS instance and class, and the session
    passes explicit per-role --window-size/--window-position (and
    --start-fullscreen for the desktop) as a fallback.
  * Fix E0283 (ambiguous `.into()`) in the missing-token error response.
  * Drop dead Value::with() helper (build warning).

 -- Debian Minerva contributors <minerva@example.org>  Mon, 27 Oct 2026 21:20:00 +0700

debian-minerva (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Real desktop session on X11: Openbox window manager, Minerva shell as
    native X windows (desktop layer, always-on-top status bar, full-width
    taskbar dock), on-demand panel windows (launcher, Wi-Fi, audio, battery,
    calendar, power, notifications, settings) opened by the daemon.
  * Real applications: the launcher lists installed .desktop entries; the
    daemon spawns real processes (terminal, file manager, browser, ...) and
    tracks them for dock running indicators.
  * Real system control: volume via pactl/amixer, Wi-Fi scan/connect via
    nmcli, resolution via xrandr, brightness via sysfs/xrandr, night light,
    bluetooth rfkill, session power commands (lock/logout/reboot/shutdown).
  * Functional Settings window: appearance (theme/accent/wallpaper/scale),
    display (real resolution list + apply), sound, network, about.
  * Software app now searches the real Debian archive (apt-cache) and
    installs via a real terminal running sudo apt.
  * Removed: boot animation, first-run wizard, "Rust core" dock badge,
    decorative status-bar buttons (sync/location/record/lang) and the
    aggregate quick-settings panel — replaced by per-icon real popovers.
  * minerva-ctl: CLI for keybinds/root menu to drive the session daemon.

